WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Welcome to the Reliable Agent Capstone.
Your goal is not

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.800
to build the largest or most autonomous
agent. Your goal

3
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:19.200
is to prove that one useful workflow can
be understood,

4
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:25.600
bounded, tested, observed, recovered,
revised, and handed to another operator

5
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:32.000
with evidence they can independently
review.

6
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.429
Choose a bounded mission whose effects can
be simulated or

7
00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:42.857
safely reversed. Define the user, desired
outcome, inputs, non-goals, acceptance

8
00:00:42.857 --> 00:00:48.286
criteria, stop conditions, and residual
risk. Write the state model

9
00:00:48.286 --> 00:00:53.714
before selecting a provider or model. At
minimum, distinguish intake,

10
00:00:53.714 --> 00:00:59.143
validation, planning, authorization,
execution, verification, reconciliation,

11
00:00:59.143 --> 00:01:04.571
completion, and failure. Name the durable
record that proves every

12
00:01:04.571 --> 00:01:10.000
transition. Completion is not a model
statement; it is an

13
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.429
observed postcondition tied to the
workflow state. Keep portable

14
00:01:15.429 --> 00:01:20.857
responsibilities above provider adapters.
Anthropic, OpenAI, and Google

15
00:01:20.857 --> 00:01:26.286
implementations may expose different
tools, tracing objects, or orchestration

16
00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:31.714
features, but none may silently change
authority, evidence, or terminal-state

17
00:01:31.714 --> 00:01:37.143
rules. If a reviewer cannot say what the
workflow may

18
00:01:37.143 --> 00:01:42.571
change, when it must stop, and how
completion is proven,

19
00:01:42.571 --> 00:01:48.000
narrow the mission before continuing.

20
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.429
Inventory every model, tool, data source,
credential, human role, and

21
00:01:53.429 --> 00:01:58.857
destination. For each tool, record allowed
and denied operations, input

22
00:01:58.857 --> 00:02:04.286
validation, object authorization,
approval, execution limits, idempotency,

23
00:02:04.286 --> 00:02:09.714
postcondition, audit event, and recovery.
Draw trust boundaries around user

24
00:02:09.714 --> 00:02:15.143
input, retrieved content, model output,
MCP servers, memory, secret-bearing

25
00:02:15.143 --> 00:02:20.571
executors, and external systems.
Instructions inside data remain untrusted

26
00:02:20.571 --> 00:02:26.000
data until a trusted control plane
validates them. Threat-model prompt

27
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.429
injection, confused-deputy action,
excessive permission, secret exposure,

28
00:02:31.429 --> 00:02:36.857
replay, duplicate writes, poisoned memory,
unsafe delegation, and misleading success.

29
00:02:36.857 --> 00:02:42.286
Every material threat needs prevention,
detection, containment, and recovery. The

30
00:02:42.286 --> 00:02:47.714
model may propose an action, but only the
trusted executor

31
00:02:47.714 --> 00:02:53.143
resolves identity and tenant, enforces
policy, obtains required approval,

32
00:02:53.143 --> 00:02:58.571
performs the bounded effect, and verifies
the result. Confidence never

33
00:02:58.571 --> 00:03:04.000
grants authority.

34
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.429
Engineer the minimum context for each
step: objective, constraints,

35
00:03:09.429 --> 00:03:14.857
authoritative evidence, current state,
tool contract, output schema, budget, and

36
00:03:14.857 --> 00:03:20.286
escalation rule. Exclude stale,
irrelevant, unrelated, and secret

37
00:03:20.286 --> 00:03:25.714
material. Separate working context from
durable memory. Define what may

38
00:03:25.714 --> 00:03:31.143
be remembered, lawful purpose, reader,
source of truth, correction path,

39
00:03:31.143 --> 00:03:36.571
expiration, deletion, and conflict
behavior. For MCP connections, record

40
00:03:36.571 --> 00:03:42.000
server identity, negotiated capabilities,
authorization, data sent, tool contracts,

41
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:47.429
approval, postconditions, and fallback.
For multi-agent handoffs, transfer a

42
00:03:47.429 --> 00:03:52.857
versioned packet with goal, trusted facts,
unresolved questions, completed effects,

43
00:03:52.857 --> 00:03:58.286
allowed and denied actions, budget,
acceptance checks, return states, and

44
00:03:58.286 --> 00:04:03.714
trace. The recipient must be able to
reject an incomplete,

45
00:04:03.714 --> 00:04:09.143
stale, misrouted, or over-privileged
packet without guessing. A handoff

46
00:04:09.143 --> 00:04:14.571
transfers a contract with evidence, not a
conversation dump or

47
00:04:14.571 --> 00:04:20.000
hidden authority.

48
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:25.429
Evaluate success and exercise failure.
Build representative routine cases,

49
00:04:25.429 --> 00:04:30.857
boundary cases, adversarial inputs, and
known failures. Use deterministic checks

50
00:04:30.857 --> 00:04:36.286
for schemas, permissions, tool arguments,
approvals, operation keys, postconditions,

51
00:04:36.286 --> 00:04:41.714
terminal states, latency, and cost. Use
calibrated human review for

52
00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:47.143
judgment. Test tool denial, malformed
output, timeout, partial write, duplicate

53
00:04:47.143 --> 00:04:52.571
request, stale context, poisoned
instruction, provider unavailability, and

54
00:04:52.571 --> 00:04:58.000
missing telemetry. Write expected
containment before execution and record

55
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:03.429
the observed result. Never retry an
uncertain external action until

56
00:05:03.429 --> 00:05:08.857
the system of record reconciles its state.
A retry must

57
00:05:08.857 --> 00:05:14.286
be idempotent or protected by a durable
operation key, and

58
00:05:14.286 --> 00:05:19.714
recovery evidence must prove it did not
duplicate or conceal

59
00:05:19.714 --> 00:05:25.143
an effect. Compare the candidate with a
baseline on identical

60
00:05:25.143 --> 00:05:30.571
versioned cases and preserve every input
needed for reproduction and

61
00:05:30.571 --> 00:05:36.000
rollback.

62
00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:41.429
Design observability and the operating
runbook together. Correlate workflow,

63
00:05:41.429 --> 00:05:46.857
agent, model, retrieval, tool, handoff,
approval, verification, and outcome

64
00:05:46.857 --> 00:05:52.286
events. Record versions, timing, state
transitions, policy decisions, failure

65
00:05:52.286 --> 00:05:57.714
classes, resource use, and secure evidence
references. Exclude or redact

66
00:05:57.714 --> 00:06:03.143
prompts, secrets, personal data, sensitive
tool payloads, and hidden reasoning.

67
00:06:03.143 --> 00:06:08.571
Define service indicators that expose user
harm or control failure:

68
00:06:08.571 --> 00:06:14.000
evaluation regression, policy denial,
incomplete trace, duplicate-effect

69
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:19.429
attempt, unresolved reconciliation, unsafe
escalation, and learner-evidence integrity

70
00:06:19.429 --> 00:06:24.857
failure. The runbook covers detection,
severity, containment, evidence

71
00:06:24.857 --> 00:06:30.286
preservation, reconciliation, safe retry,
rollback, escalation, communication,

72
00:06:30.286 --> 00:06:35.714
recovery verification, and post-incident
improvement. Name the owner, authority,

73
00:06:35.714 --> 00:06:41.143
exact target, evidence required, and
fallback at each decision. A

74
00:06:41.143 --> 00:06:46.571
healthy endpoint is insufficient if
external state or the learner

75
00:06:46.571 --> 00:06:52.000
record remains wrong.

76
00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.211
Submit eight versioned artifacts:
architecture and state model; tool

77
00:06:56.211 --> 00:07:00.421
inventory and permission matrix;
trust-boundary and threat model;

78
00:07:00.421 --> 00:07:04.632
evaluation set and rubric; failure tests
and results; observability plan;

79
00:07:04.632 --> 00:07:08.842
operating runbook; and evidence map with
operational handoff. Use the

80
00:07:08.842 --> 00:07:13.053
stable filenames
architecture-and-state-model.md,

81
00:07:13.053 --> 00:07:17.263
tool-inventory-and-permission-matrix.md,
trust-boundary-and-threat-model.md,

82
00:07:17.263 --> 00:07:21.474
evaluation-set-and-rubric.json,
failure-tests-and-results.md,

83
00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:25.684
observability-plan.md,
operating-runbook.md, and

84
00:07:25.684 --> 00:07:29.895
evidence-map-and-handoff.md. Map each of
six rubric criteria to exact artifact

85
00:07:29.895 --> 00:07:34.105
or knowledge-check references. Correctness
and safety are worth twenty points

86
00:07:34.105 --> 00:07:38.316
each. Evidence quality and maintainability
are worth fifteen each. Reliability

87
00:07:38.316 --> 00:07:42.526
is worth twenty, and communication is
worth ten. A score

88
00:07:42.526 --> 00:07:46.737
without references is invalid. Compare the
complete and flawed exemplars

89
00:07:46.737 --> 00:07:50.947
by evidence, not polish. The flawed
example has broad authority,

90
00:07:50.947 --> 00:07:55.158
three easy cases, blind retry, invasive
telemetry, and no actionable

91
00:07:55.158 --> 00:07:59.368
runbook even though its language sounds
confident. Preserve the first

92
00:07:59.368 --> 00:08:03.579
submission, criterion feedback, revised
artifacts, changed evidence map, and final

93
00:08:03.579 --> 00:08:07.789
handoff. Completion requires both an
eighty-percent knowledge check and an

94
00:08:07.789 --> 00:08:12.000
applied capstone score of at least eighty
percent.

95
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:17.077
Compare two support-triage packages. The
complete package uses synthetic tickets,

96
00:08:17.077 --> 00:08:22.154
explicit states, a durable case and
operation key, human approval

97
00:08:22.154 --> 00:08:27.231
before sandbox send, one-object
permissions, nine failure tests, redacted

98
00:08:27.231 --> 00:08:32.308
traces, destination read-back, and an
owned runbook. Every score points

99
00:08:32.308 --> 00:08:37.385
to artifacts and test identifiers. The
flawed package says the

100
00:08:37.385 --> 00:08:42.462
agent resolves tickets, grants all tools,
trusts user text, asks

101
00:08:42.462 --> 00:08:47.538
the same model to judge three easy cases,
retries every

102
00:08:47.538 --> 00:08:52.615
timeout, stores prompts and credentials
forever, and declares success because

103
00:08:52.615 --> 00:08:57.692
the demo looked good. Its polish cannot
compensate for missing

104
00:08:57.692 --> 00:09:02.769
state, authority, failure evidence,
privacy, or recovery. Use the flawed

105
00:09:02.769 --> 00:09:07.846
exemplar to locate the weakest criterion
in your own first

106
00:09:07.846 --> 00:09:12.923
submission, revise that evidence, and
explain the change in the

107
00:09:12.923 --> 00:09:18.000
handoff.

108
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:25.000
Name the most consequential effect your
workflow could attempt. Identify

109
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:32.000
the trusted executor, exact permission,
approval, operation key, postcondition,

110
00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:39.000
containment control, and recovery evidence
that make the effect bounded.

111
00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:15.000
Checkpoint. A reviewer believes the
workflow is safe but cannot

112
00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:21.000
link the safety score to a submitted
artifact or assessment

113
00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:27.000
result. Is the score valid?

114
00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:32.250
The score is invalid. Reviewer confidence
cannot replace criterion evidence.

115
00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:37.500
Link safety points to the permission
matrix, threat model, containment

116
00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:42.750
test, privacy controls, approval record,
or relevant assessment result. If

117
00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:48.000
the evidence does not exist, lower the
score and revise

118
00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:53.250
the package. If you supplied one overall
screenshot, split it

119
00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:58.500
into stable artifact and test references.
The evidence map must

120
00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:03.750
let another reviewer reproduce why each
point was awarded without

121
00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:09.000
hidden reasoning.

122
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:16.000
Open the reliable-agent capstone. Produce
all eight artifacts, execute routine,

123
00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:23.000
adversarial, and recovery tests, define
privacy-aware telemetry and the runbook,

124
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:30.000
map all six rubric criteria to evidence,
self-score against both

125
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:37.000
exemplars, submit, preserve feedback,
revise failing evidence, and deliver the

126
00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:44.000
final operational handoff with residual
risk.

127
00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:55.000
When ready, begin the knowledge check. You
will prove writes

128
00:17:55.000 --> 00:18:02.000
with durable evidence, reconcile timeouts,
require criterion-level references, use

129
00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:09.000
the flawed exemplar for calibration, and
apply the dual eighty-percent

130
00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:16.000
completion gate. Then return to the
versioned capstone submission.

131
00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:22.000
A reliable agent is bounded by state,
authority, evidence, evaluation,

132
00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:28.000
privacy-aware observability, and tested
recovery. Preserve failed and revised

133
00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:34.000
attempts so mastery reflects improvement,
not hidden replacement.
